{"name":"Purple Thorn","hex":"#f0b9be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"thorn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A modified branch that is hard and sharp like a spike.","Any thorn-like structure on plants, such as the spine and the prickle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pierce with, or as if with, a thorn (sharp pointed object)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thorn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Purple thorn","blocks":[{"text":"The purple thorn is a moth of the family Geometridae. The species was first described by Johann Siegfried Hufnagel in 1767. It is a species of both Northern Europe and Central Europe. It has a scattered distribution in Britain but is absent from Ireland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Selenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_dos.jpg/330px-Selenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_dos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple_thorn"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Selenia.tetralunaria.7138.jpg/500px-Selenia.tetralunaria.7138.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Selenia.tetralunaria.7138.jpg/1280px-Selenia.tetralunaria.7138.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Selenia.tetralunaria.7138.jpg/500px-Selenia.tetralunaria.7138.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASelenia.tetralunaria.7138.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Selenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_ventre.jpg/500px-Selenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_ventre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Selenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_ventre.jpg/1280px-Selenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_ventre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Selenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_ventre.jpg/500px-Selenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_ventre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Male underside","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASelenia_tetralunaria_MHNT_ventre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Buckler_W_The_larv%C3%A6_of_the_British_butterflies_and_moths_PlateCVII.jpg/500px-Buckler_W_The